# The trial of pod-ws in podnet: src/ws.rs keeps podnet's words and the
# edge side (serve_websocket, forward_path, forward_url, LocalSpec) and
# takes the WebSocket of pod-ws: the client of `podnet connect` (its dial,
# with Authorization and the limits of tokio-tungstenite, and its bridge),
# the server session of the forward endpoint and its bridge, accept_key and
# close_hint. The relay client keeps its bridge of tokio-tungstenite until
# pod-relay. Each podcrates tag moves to the tag of the hand-off. The
# record, the size and the layers of the files, the build, the bans and the
# sources of cargo-deny, clippy, the tests of the library, the integration
# tests of connect (a client of pod-ws against a server of
# tokio-tungstenite), the edge, TLS and the reverse relay, the fuzz targets
# with their lock, rustfmt, each Rust toolchain of the workflows and build
# images against the rust-version of podcrates, and the binary for x86_64
# musl, built with zig (a debug build: the release profile takes LTO), with
# podnet's static check of it.
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-size.py
python3 scripts/check-layers.py
cargo build -q
command -v cargo-deny > /dev/null || cargo install -q --locked cargo-deny
cargo deny --locked check bans sources
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podnet -p podnet-netns -p podnet-core -- -D warnings
cargo test -q -p podnet --lib
cargo test -q -p podnet --test connect --test egress --test tls --test relay_reverse --test cli --test api_surface
cargo update -q -w --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml
cargo check -q --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml --bins
cargo fmt --all --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
cargo zigbuild -q --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -p podnet --bin podnet
sh scripts/check-static.sh "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podnet"
